  "headline": "The Temple City",
  "short_description": "Madurai is built around the towering gopurams of the Meenakshi Amman Temple and is one of Tamil Nadu's oldest continuously inhabited cities.",
  "about": "One of the oldest cities in the Indian subcontinent, Madurai has been a centre of Tamil culture, trade and Dravidian temple architecture for over two millennia.\n\nLocated on the banks of the Vaigai river in southern Tamil Nadu.\n\nA living centre of Tamil literature, classical arts and temple ritual traditions.\n\nA major Hindu pilgrimage centre, home to the Meenakshi Amman Temple dedicated to Parvati and Shiva.",
  "history": "A historic capital of the Pandya dynasty, and later ruled by the Madurai Nayaks who built much of the current Meenakshi Amman Temple complex.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Madurai Airport (airport)\n- Madurai Junction (railway)\n- Mattuthavani Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Tamil, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "1–2 days",
